<title>SWEDEN: Norgeskreditt issues $250 mln revolver.</title>
<headline>Norgeskreditt issues $250 mln revolver.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Norgeskreditt issued a $250 million multi-currency revolving credit facility, arrangers Christiania Bank of Kreditkasse and WestLB group said on Thursday. Vereins-und Westbank has joined as a co-arranger.  </p>
<p>Christiania Bank said Den Danske Bank, Norddeutsche Landsbank and Societe Generale joined prior to syndication as senior lead managers.</p>
<p>Maturity of the credit is seven years, margin is 15 basis points for years one to five and 17.5 basis points for years six and seven. The committment fee is 45 percent of the margin.</p>
<p>The borrower is a Norwegian mortgage institution owned 100 percent by Christiania Bank. Proceeds will be used as a standby facility.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
